        "body": "23 nickels would be worth 115 cents, which is $455 - 115 = 340$ cents too little. Swapping a nickel for a quarter adds 20 cents, so we need $340 \\div 20 = 17$ swaps: 17 quarters. (Check: $17 \\times 25 + 6 \\times 5 = 425 + 30 = 455$.)\n\n**Answer: (B) 17**"
